description:
Now that you've learned all this new stuff, it's time for me to say: _**Don't use it!**_. Well, not really. Actually, just don't use it _literally everywhere you can_. Instead, there is somthing that will replace inheritance sometimes: That is called _composition_. Composition is instead of creating a new, child class for each new feature the parent has, you just make a object/class that _might exist_ _inside of that object/class_, which houses a additional idea. Most of the time this is obvious when you use it instead of inheritance, but sometimes you use _**both at once!**_.
---
First, here is a example for why you would use composition _over_ inheritance.
Let's say you have a class, car.
```ts
class Car {
    doors: number;
    horsepower: number;
    color: string;
    isDrivable: boolean;
    constructor(doors: number, horsepower: number, color: string, isDrivable: boolean) {        this.doors = doors;
        this.horsepower = horsepower;
        this.color = color;
        this.isDrivable = isDrivable;
    }
}
```
Now, let's say we later want to allow cars to be convertibles. What makes more sense?
## A: Inheritance
```ts
class ConvertibleCar extends Car {
    roofOpen: boolean;
    public openRoof() {
        this.roofOpen = true;
    }
    public closeRoof() {
        this.roofOpen = false;
    }
}
```
## B: Composition
```ts
class Roof {
    isOpen: boolean;
    private isConvertible: boolean;
    constructor(isConvertible: boolean) {
        this.isConvertible = isConvertible;
    }

    public open() {
        if (this.isConvertible) {
            this.isOpen = true;
        }
    }
    public close() {
        if (this.isConvertible) {
                    this.isOpen = false;
        }
    }
}
class Car {
    roof: Roof;
    constructor(/* Same */, isConvertible: boolean) {
        this.roof = new Roof(isConvertible);
        // Stays the same
    }
    // Rest of class stays the same.
}
```
The second one, right?
Imagine needing to constantly swap between classes. That would be horrible! Also, think, The problem is: a convertible isn't a different type of car — it's a feature a car can have.
---
## Assignment:
At MeTube, we have a class, Video. However, we just added a new video type, movie! They are just videos but with a isMovie, and a lengthInHours method. What should we use, inheritance, or composition?
